<article class="env-definition" id="0657">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0657">Definition <span data-tag="0657">15.76.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Denote $D(R)$ the derived category of the abelian category of $R$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An object $K$ of $D(R)$ is <em>perfect</em> if it is quasi-isomorphic to a bounded complex of finite projective $R$-modules. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
An $R$-module $M$ is <em>perfect</em> if $M[0]$ is a perfect object in $D(R)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>